{"explanation":"A secant line passes through two points, P = (a, f(a)) and Q = (a + h, f(a + h)), with slope [f(a + h) − f(a)]/h. As h approaches 0, Q approaches P and the secant slope approaches the derivative f′(a), giving the tangent line. Drag the yellow point toward the blue point to explore this limit from either side.","manimCode":"const title = new Text({ text: 'From secant to tangent', fontSize: 34, color: WHITE });
